rpendicular to the radius at that point is the tangent at the point. Hence the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to \\((BEF)\\) at the point where it meets the circle, i.e. at the point \\(P\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCombining Lemmas\u202f1\u20135 we obtain that the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) which is parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). This completes the proof. \u220e"
