is condition. **Justification Gap.** Even if we accept the gap, the preceding equality needed to apply it is not established.\n\n---\n\n### Overall Assessment\nThe solution contains several **critical logical and factual errors** (most notably the false claim that the circumcenter \\(P\\) lies on \\(MN\\) and the incorrect derivation of power formulas) and a **justification gap** in the final tangency argument. Because the core lemmas are invalid, the proof does not establish the required statement. Hence the solution is not correct."
