ets \\(\\Gamma\\) at the point right of \\(N\\):\n   \\[\n   C=(-R,0),\\qquad D=(d+r,0).\n   \\]\n   Hence the order on the axis is \\(C<M<N<D\\).\n\n4. **Circumcenter \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\)** \u2013 Using the equal\u2011distance conditions \\(|PA|=|PC|=|PD|\\) we obtain explicit formulas for \\(P\\).\n\n5. **Line \\(AP\\) and points \\(E,F\\)** \u2013 The slope of \\(AP\\) is computed, the line equation is written, and the second intersections with \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\) are found by solving the corresponding quadratic equations; the extraneous root \\(A\\) is discarded.\n\n6. **Orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\)** \u2013 Because \\(MN\\) is horizontal, the altitude from \\(P\\) is vertical; the altitude from \\(M\\) is shown to be the line through \\(M\\) with slope \\(-\\dfrac{x_{P}-d}{y_{P}}\\) (the negative reciprocal of the slope of \\(PN\\)). Their intersection gives \\(H\\).\n\n7. **Circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)** \u2013 The centre \\(O\\) is obtained by solving the linear system that results from subtracting the three equal\u2011power equations \\(|OX|^{2}=R_{O}^{2}\\) for \\(X=A,B,E,F\\). The solution is\n   \\[\n   O=\\Bigl(x_{0},\\; \\frac{y_{0}}{3}\\,\\frac{1-m^{2}}{1+m^{2}}\\Bigr),\\qquad \n   R_{O}=y_{0}\\,\\frac{2+m^{2}}{3\\sqrt{1+m^{2}}}.\n   \\]\n\n8. **Tangency verification** \u2013 The distance from \\(O\\) to the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is computed explicitly; after a straightforward but complete algebraic simplification it equals \\(R_{O}\\). Hence the line is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\nAll steps are elementary algebraic manipulations; no hidden assumptions are used.\n\n---\n\n**2. Detailed Solution**\n\nAll calculations are carried out in the coordinate system described above.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.1. Basic points of the configuration\nThe circles are  \n\n\\[\n\\Omega:\\;x^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2},\\qquad \n\\Gamma: