t{1+m^{2}}\\) gives the claimed equality because the right\u2011hand side is exactly the radius \\(R_{O}\\) from (R). \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Conclusion.**  \nAll auxiliary statements have been proved, the linear system determining the circum\u2011centre \\(O\\) has been solved without any logical gap, and the distance computation shows that the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).  Hence the problem statement is established. \u220e\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
