nt to a circle at a point \\(Y\\) iff the angle that the line makes with the chord \\(YZ\\) equals the angle subtended by the same chord at the opposite point of the circle.  \n\nHence the line through \\(H\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) makes with the chord \\(BE\\) the angle \\(\\angle BFE\\); consequently it is tangent to the circumcircle \\((BEF)\\).\n\n\u220e\n"
