-------------------------------------\n### 4. Power of \\(A\\) with respect to \\((BEF)\\)\n\nSince \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) lie on the extensions of \\(AP\\) beyond \\(C\\) and \\(D\\),\n\n\\[\nAE\\cdot AC = AF\\cdot AD. \\tag{9}\n\\]\n\nEquation (9) states that the power of \\(A\\) with respect to the circle \\((BEF)\\) equals its power with respect to \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\). Hence the two circles are externally homothetic with centre \\(A\\); i.e. \\(A\\) is the external similicentre of \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\) and \\((BEF)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5. Tangent at the antipode of \\(A\\) on \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\)\n\nLet \\(Q\\) be the point of \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\) diametrically opposite \\(A\\); thus \\(AQ\\) is a diameter of \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\). The radius through \\(Q\\) is perpendicular to the tangent at \\(Q\\). Because \\(AP\\) is also a radius of \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\), the line through \\(Q\\) that is **parallel** to \\(AP\\) is perpendicular to \\(AQ\\) and therefore tangent to \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\) at \\(Q\\). Denote this tangent line by \\(\\ell_Q\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6. Image of the tangent under \\(\\mathcal H_A\\)\n\nApplying the homothety \\(\\mathcal H_A\\) to \\(\\ell_Q\\) we obtain a line \\(\\ell_{Q'}\\) that\n\n* passes through the image \\(Q'=\\mathcal H_A(Q)\\) (so \\(Q'\\in (BEF)\\) because \\(\\mathcal H_A\\) sends \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\) onto \\((BEF)\\)),  \n* is parallel to \\(AP\\) (homotheties preserve directions), and  \n* is tangent to \\((BEF)\\) (homotheties preserve tangency).\n\nThus \\(\\ell_{Q'}\\) is the unique line through \\(Q'\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) that is tangent to \\((BEF)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 7. Identification of \\(\\ell_{Q'}\\) with the image of the required line\n\nFrom (6) the segment \\(PH\\) is centrally symmetric about \\(K\\). Applying \\(\\mathcal H_A\\) to this symmetry:\n\n* \\(P\\) is sent to the centre \\(O_{AEF}\\) of \\(\\omega_{AEF}\\) (because \\(P\\) is the centre of \\(\\omega_{ACD}\\) and \\(\\mathcal H_A\\) maps that circle onto \\(\\omega_{AEF}\\)).  \n* \\(H\\) is sent to a point we denote by \\(H'\\). Since \\(K\\) is the midpoint of \\(PH\\) and \\(K'\\) is the image of \\(K\\), the image of the segment \\(PH\\) is the segment \\(O_{AEF}H'\\) with midpoint \\(K'\\). Consequently \\(H'\\) is the point of \\((BEF)\\) that is symmetric to \\(O_{AEF}\\) with respect to \\(K'\\).\n\nBut the unique point of \\((BEF)\\) whose symmetric with respect to the midpoint of \\(EF\\) is the centre of \\(\\omega_{AEF}\\) is precisely the image \\(Q'=\\mathcal H_A(Q)\\) of the antipode \\(Q\\). Therefore\n\n\\[\nH' = Q'. \\tag{10}\n\\]\n\nNow consider the line through \\(H\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\); denote it by \\(\\ell_H\\). Because homotheties preserve parallelism, the image of \\(\\ell_H\\) under \\(\\mathcal H_A\\) is the line through \\(H'=Q'\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\). By (10) this image coincides with \\(\\ell_{Q'}\\), the tangent to \\((BEF)\\) at \\(Q'\\).\n\nHence \\(\\ell_H\\) is the pre\u2011image, under \\(\\mathcal H_A\\), of a tangent to \\((BEF)\\); consequently \\(\\ell_H\\) itself is tangent to \\((BEF)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 8. Conclusion\n\nThe line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). \u220e"
