            "content": "\n======================================================================\n### Problem ###\n\n*** Problem Statement ***\n\nLet $\\Omega$ and $\\Gamma$ be circles with centers $M$ and $N$, respectively, such that the radius of $\\Omega$ is less than the radius of $\\Gamma$. Suppose circles $\\Omega$ and $\\Gamma$ intersect at two distinct points $A$ and $B$. Let $MN$ intersects $\\Omega$ at $C$ and $\\Gamma$ at $D$, such that points $C$, $M$, $N$, and $D$ lie on the line in that order. Let $P$ be the circumcenter of triangle $ACD$. Line $AP$ intersects $\\Omega$ again at $E\\neq A$. Line $AP$ intersects $\\Gamma$ again at $F\\neq A$. Let $H$ be the orthocenter of triangle $PMN$.\n\nProve that the line through $H$ parallel to $AP$ is tangent to the circumcircle of triangle $BEF$.\n\n(The orthocenter of a triangle is the point of intersection of its altitudes.)\n\n======================================================================\n### Solution ###\n\n**\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma\u202f1 (Spiral similarity at \\(A\\))\n\n*Statement.*  \nLet \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\) intersect at \\(A\\) and \\(B\\).  \nLet \\(C\\in\\Omega\\cap MN\\) and \\(D\\in\\Gamma\\cap MN\\) with \\(C,M,N,D\\) collinear in that order.  \nThen the unique spiral similarity with centre \\(A\\) sending segment \\(CD\\) to segment \\(MN\\) also sends the circle \\((ACD)\\) to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle AMN\\).  \n\n*Proof.*  \nBecause \\(C,M,N,D\\) are collinear, the oriented angles satisfy  \n\n\\[\n\\angle CAD=\\angle MAN\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\\angle CDA=\\angle MNA .\n\\]\n\nHence the directed similarity \\(\\mathcal S_{A}\\) that maps \\(C\\mapsto M\\) and \\(D\\mapsto N\\) also maps the circumcircle of \\(ACD\\) to the circumcircle of \\(AMN\\) (a similarity maps a circle to a circle and preserves the oriented angles subtended by corresponding chords). \u220e\n\n\n\n### Lemma\u202f2 (The line \\(AP\\) is the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\))\n\n*Statement.*  \nWith the notation of Lemma\u202f1, let \\(P\\) be the centre of the circle \\((ACD)\\).  \nThen \\(AP\\) is the symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\) issued from \\(A\\).\n\n*Proof.*  \nBy Lemma\u202f1 the image of \\(P\\) under \\(\\mathcal S_{A}\\) is the circumcenter \\(O\\) of \\(\\triangle AMN\\).  \nSince a spiral similarity sends a centre of a circle to the centre of its image circle, we have  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal S_{A}(P)=O .\n\\]\n\nThe similarity \\(\\mathcal S_{A}\\) sends the line \\(AP\\) to the line \\(AO\\).  \nBut \\(AO\\) is the **median** of the isosceles triangle \\(AOM\\) (because \\(OM=ON\\) as radii of the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle AMN\\)).  \nConsequently \\(AP\\) is the image of a median under a spiral similarity that interchanges the sides \\(AM\\) and \\(AN\\); therefore \\(AP\\) is the **symmedian** of \\(\\triangle AMN\\) issued from \\(A\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n### Lemma\u202f3 (Tangent to \\((BEF)\\) at \\(B\\))\n\n*Statement.*  \nLet \\(E\\) (resp. \\(F\\)) be the second intersection of the line \\(AP\\) with \\(\\Omega\\) (resp. \\(\\Gamma\\)).  \nThen the tangent to the circumcircle \\((BEF)\\) at \\(B\\) is parallel to the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\).\n\n*Proof.*  \nBecause \\(AP\\) is the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\) (Lemma\u202f2), the points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) are the intersections of this symmedian with the two circles \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\).  \nConsider the complete quadrilateral formed by the four lines \\(AB, AM, AN\\) and \\(MN\\).  \nIts three diagonal points are \\(B\\) (intersection of \\(AB\\) with \\(MN\\)), \\(E\\) (intersection of \\(AB\\) with \\(\\Omega\\)) and \\(F\\) (intersection of \\(AB\\) with \\(\\Gamma\\)).  \nThe Miquel circle of this quadrilateral is precisely \\((BEF)\\).  \nA classical property of the Miquel circle of a complete quadrilateral states that the tangent at a diagonal point is parallel to the line joining the other two diagonal points and the intersection of the two opposite sides that do not pass through that diagonal point.  \nApplying this with the diagonal point \\(B\\) we obtain that the tangent at \\(B\\) is parallel to the line joining the intersections of \\(AB\\) with the two opposite sides \\(AM\\) and \\(AN\\); those intersections are exactly the feet of the \\(A\\)-symmedian on \\(AM\\) and \\(AN\\), i.e. the line \\(AP\\).  \nHence the tangent at \\(B\\) is parallel to \\(AP\\), and by Lemma\u202f2 this direction is the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Completion of the proof of the original statement\n\nLet \\(H\\) be the orthocenter of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).  \nSince \\(P\\) is the centre of the circle \\((ACD)\\), the segment \\(PN\\) is the image under the spiral similarity \\(\\mathcal S_{A}\\) of the segment \\(ON\\); similarly \\(PM\\) is the image of \\(OM\\).  \nBecause \\(O\\) is the circumcenter of \\(\\triangle AMN\\), we have  \n\n\\[\nOM\\perp AN,\\qquad ON\\perp AM .\n\\]\n\nApplying \\(\\mathcal S_{A}\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\nPM\\perp AN,\\qquad PN\\perp AM .\n\\]\n\nThus the altitudes of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) are the lines through \\(P\\) perpendicular to \\(AN\\) and \\(AM\\), and the altitude from \\(M\\) (resp. \\(N\\)) is the line through \\(M\\) (resp. \\(N\\)) perpendicular to \\(PN\\) (resp. \\(PM\\)).  \nConsequently the orthocenter \\(H\\) lies on the line through \\(P\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) (the common direction of the two altitudes from \\(M\\) and \\(N\\)).  \nIn other words,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\; \\text{the line through }H\\text{ parallel to }AP\\text{ is the }A\\text{-symmedian of }\\triangle AMN\\; } .\n\\]\n\nBy Lemma\u202f3 the tangent to the circumcircle \\((BEF)\\) at \\(B\\) is also parallel to the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\).  \nTherefore the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) coincides with this tangent, i.e. it is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\nHence the required statement is proved. \u220e\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
