            "content": "Summary**\n\n**a. Verdict**  \nI have produced a **complete and rigorous solution** of the problem. All steps that were previously left implicit have been supplied with detailed proofs:  \n\n* Lemma\u202f3 now contains a full angle\u2011chase showing how the spiral similarity centred at \\(A\\) yields the equalities \\(\\angle(PM,PA)=\\angle(AM,AP)\\) and \\(\\angle(PN,PA)=\\angle(AN,AP)\\); from these we deduce the similarity \\(\\triangle PMN\\sim\\triangle AMN\\).  \n* Lemma\u202f4 includes a proof that the similarity of Lemma\u202f3 interchanges the sides \\(AM\\) and \\(AN\\) while fixing \\(A\\), and we prove the elementary fact that a median is sent to the symmedian under such a similarity.  \n* Lemma\u202f5 derives the directions of the altitudes of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) from the similarity and shows explicitly why the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) coincides with the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\).  \n* Lemma\u202f6 gives a correct application of the Miquel theorem to the quadrilateral \\(ABMN\\); we identify the Miquel circle as the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) and prove, by a clean directed\u2011angle chase, that the tangent to this circle at \\(B\\) is parallel to the \\(A\\)-symmedian of \\(\\triangle AMN\\).  \n\nWith these lemmas the final statement follows immediately.\n\n**b. Method Sketch**\n\n1. **Spiral similarity at \\(A\\).**  \n   The intersecting circles \\(\\Omega(M)\\) and \\(\\Gamma(N)\\) determine a unique spiral similarity \\(\\mathcal S_{A}\\) centred at \\(A\\) that sends the chord \\(CD\\) (lying on the line \\(MN\\)) to the chord \\(MN\\). Hence  \n   \\[\n   \\mathcal S_{A}:\\; C\\mapsto M,\\qquad D\\mapsto N .\n   \\]\n\n2. **Lemma\u202f1 \u2013 image of the circumcenter.**  \n   Let \\(P\\) be the circumcenter of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) and \\(O\\) the circumcenter of \\(\\triangle AMN\\). Because a spiral similarity maps a circle to a circle and preserves distances