-------------------------------------------------\n### Completion of the proof\n\nFrom Lemma\u202f1, \\(AP\\) is the internal bisector of \\(\\angle BAF\\).  \nLemma\u202f4 tells us that the line \\(\\ell\\) through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) meets the circumcircle \\((BEF)\\) at a point \\(T\\) for which \\(\\angle BTF = \\angle BAF\\).  \n\nIn a circle, the tangent at a point \\(T\\) makes an angle with a chord equal to the angle in the opposite arc. Hence the line through \\(T\\) that makes with chord \\(BF\\) an angle equal to \\(\\angle BAF\\) is precisely the tangent to \\((BEF)\\) at \\(T\\). Because \\(\\ell\\) passes through \\(T\\) and is parallel to \\(AP\\), and \\(\\angle BAF\\) is the angle between \\(AP\\) and chord \\(BF\\), we conclude that \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\nSince \\(\\ell\\) is the line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\), the statement to be proved follows. \u220e"
