ery admissible configuration of the two intersecting circles.\n\nTherefore the line \\(y=m_{AP}x\\), i.e. the line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\), touches the circumcircle (10) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) at a single point.  \n\n\u220e\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion**  \nThe orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) coincides with the origin in the chosen coordinate system; the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) has equation \\(y=m_{AP}x\\).  By an explicit computation of the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) and a discriminant check, this line is shown to be tangent to that circle.  Hence the statement of the problem holds for all configurations of two intersecting circles with the described construction. \u220e"
