rom the long fraction to \\(d-R\\) is not shown; this identity is later used critically.\n\n* **Location:** Derivation of (2.31): \u201c\\(m_{AP}= -\\frac{H_{x}}{d}\\).\u201d  \n  * **Issue:** Justification Gap \u2013 the proof relies on several intermediate equalities (e.g., \\(p_{x}-x_{0}=d\\)) that are never established; the conclusion is presented as a \u201cshort algebraic manipulation\u201d without details.\n\n* **Location:** Claim (2.33): \u201c\\(H_{x}= -\\dfrac{d\\,x_{0}}{R}\\).\u201d  \n  * **Issue:** Justification Gap \u2013 the substitution of the explicit forms of \\(p_{x},p_{y}\\) into (2.21) and the simplification to (2.33) are omitted; this relation is essential for the final discriminant calculation.\n\n* **Location:** Final discriminant computation (\u0394 = 0).  \n  * **Issue:** Justification Gap \u2013 the statement \u201cAfter a straightforward but careful algebraic expansion all terms cancel\u201d is not accompanied by any algebra; the cancellation depends on the previously unproved identities (2.28b) and (2.33). Without explicit computation the conclusion that the line is tangent remains unverified.\n\n* **Location:** Overall structure \u2013 the solution repeatedly declares \u201croutine but lengthy algebraic manipulation\u201d in place of detailed calculations.  \n  * **Issue:** Justification Gap \u2013 at IMO level, such manipulations must be either carried out explicitly or replaced by a clear, rigorous argument (e.g., using power of a point, similarity, or vector geometry). The reliance on omitted algebra leaves the proof incomplete.\n\n---\n\n###"
