ract the equations of the circles:\n\n\\[\n(x-d)^{2}+y^{2}-\\bigl(x^{2}+y^{2}\\bigr)=r^{2}-R^{2}\n\\Longrightarrow -2dx+d^{2}=r^{2}-R^{2}.\n\\]\n\nHence the common abscissa of the two intersection points is  \n\n\\[\nx_{0}= \\frac{d^{2}+R^{2}-r^{2}}{2d}. \\tag{2.11}\n\\]\n\nInsert \\(x_{0}\\) into \\(\\Omega\\) :\n\n\\[\ny_{0}^{2}=R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}>0,\n\\]\n\nthe strict inequality following from (2.9).  Define  \n\n\\[\nA=(x_{0},y_{0}),\\qquad B=(x_{0},-y_{0}). \\tag{2.12}\n\\]\n\nFrom the construction we have the two identities that will be used repeatedly:\n\n\\[\nx_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=R^{2},\\qquad d^{2}+R^{2}-r^{2}=2dx_{0}. \\tag{\u2605}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### 2.4  Circumcenter \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\)\n\nThe midpoint of \\(AC\\) is  \n\n\\[\nM_{AC}= \\Bigl(\\frac{x_{0}-R}{2},\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr),\n\\]\nthe slope of \\(AC\\) is \\(\\displaystyle \\frac{y_{0}}{x_{0}+R}\\); therefore the perpendicular bisector of \\(AC\\) has equation  \n\n\\[\ny-\\frac{y_{0}}{2}= -\\frac{x_{0}+R}{y_{0}}\\Bigl(x-\\frac{x_{0}-R}{2}\\Bigr). \\tag{2.13}\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, the midpoint of \\(AD\\) is  \n\n\\[\nM_{AD}= \\Bigl(\\frac{x_{0}+d+r}{2},\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr),\n\\]\nthe slope of \\(AD\\) is \\(\\displaystyle \\frac{y_{0}}{x_{0}-d-r}\\); its perpendicular bisector is  \n\n\\[\ny-\\frac{y_{0}}{2}= -\\frac{x_{0}-d-r}{y_{0}}\\Bigl(x-\\frac{x_{0}+d+r}{2}\\Bigr). \\tag{2.14}\n\\]\n\nBoth (2.13) and (2.14) are linear in \\(x,y\\).  Solving them simultaneously:\n\nFrom (2.13),\n\n\\[\ny= -\\frac{x_{0}+R}{y_{0}}x+\\frac{x_{0}^{2}-R^{2}+y_{0}^{2}}{2y_{0}}. \\tag{2.15}\n\\]\n\nFrom (2.14),\n\n\\[\ny= -\\frac{x_{0}-d-r}{y_{0}}x+\\frac{x_{0}^{2}-(d+r)^{2}+y_{0}^{2}}{2y_{0}}. \\tag{2.16}\n\\]\n\nEquating the right\u2011hand sides of (2.15) and (2.16) and multiplying by \\(2y_{0}\\) gives  \n\n\\[\n-(x_{0}+R)x+x_{0}^{2}-R^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=-(x_{0}-d-r)x+x_{0}^{2}-(d+r)^{2}+y_{0}^{2}.\n\\]\n\nCancel \\(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}\\) and