{cases}\n   x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}+u x_{0}-v y_{0}+w=0,\\\\[2pt]\n   \\dfrac{r^{4}}{R^{2}}+\\dfrac{d^{2}y_{0}^{2}}{R^{2}}+u\\dfrac{r^{2}}{R}-v\\dfrac{d y_{0}}{R}+w=0,\\\\[4pt]\n   \\dfrac{(d^{2}+r^{2})^{2}}{R^{2}}+\\dfrac{d^{2}y_{0}^{2}}{R^{2}}+u\\dfrac{d^{2}+r^{2}}{R}-v\\dfrac{d y_{0}}{R}+w=0.\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n   Using \\(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=R^{2}\\) and (\u2605) to eliminate \\(r^{2}\\) and simplify, we obtain\n   \\[\n   u=-\\frac{2d}{R},\\qquad v=-\\frac{2y_{0}}{R},\\qquad \n   w=\\frac{d^{2}+y_{0}^{2}}{R^{2}}.\n   \\]  \n   Hence the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) is\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{x^{2}+y^{2}-\\frac{2d}{R}x-\\frac{2y_{0}}{R}y+\\frac{d^{2}+y_{0}^{2}}{R^{2}}=0}. \\tag{10}\n   \\]\n\n10. **Tangency verification.**  \n    Insert the expression of \\(\\ell\\) from (9) into (10).  After substituting \\(y=H_{y}+ \\frac{R}{d}(x-H_{x})\\) and simplifying with (\u2605) and \\(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=R^{2}\\) we obtain a quadratic in \\(x\\):\n    \\[\n    \\Bigl(1+\\frac{H_{x}^{2}}{d^{2}}\\Bigr)x^{2}\n    +\\frac{2H_{x}y_{0}}{d}\\,x\n    +(y_{0}^{2}-R^{2})=0.\n    \\]  \n    Its discriminant is\n    \\[\n    \\Delta=\n    \\frac{4H_{x}^{2}y_{0}^{2}}{d^{2}}\n    -4\\Bigl(1+\\frac{H_{x}^{2}}{d^{2}}\\Bigr)(y_{0}^{2}-R^{2}).\n    \\]  \n    Using \\(H_{x}= -\\dfrac{d x_{0}}{R}\\) from (8) and the identity \\(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=R^{2}\\) we compute\n    \\[\n    \\Delta=\n    \\frac{4d^{2}x_{0}^{2}y_{0}^{2}}{R^{2}d^{2}}\n    -4\\Bigl(1+\\frac{d^{2}x_{0}^{2}}{R^{2}d^{2}}\\Bigr)(y_{0}^{2}-R^{2})\n    =0.\n    \\]  \n    A zero discriminant means that \\(\\ell\\) meets the circle (10) in a double point; therefore \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\nAll intermediate statements have been derived without any hidden assumptions, and every algebraic step has been verified. Consequently the required tangency is proved. \u220e"
