}+2m^{2}(d-x_{0})y_{0}}\n                {(d-x_{0})+my_{0}},\\qquad\n   f_{y}=y_{0}+m(f_{x}-x_{0}).\n   \\]\n\n7. **Circle \\((BEF)\\)** \u2013 The general equation of a circle is \\(x^{2}+y^{2}+ux+vy+w=0\\).  \n   Substituting the coordinates of \\(B,E,F\\) gives a linear system for \\(u,v,w\\). Solving yields the centre\n   \\[\n   O_{BEF}=(x_{c},y_{c})=\n          \\Bigl(\\frac{x_{0}+e_{x}+f_{x}}{3},\n                \\frac{-y_{0}+e_{y}+f_{y}}{3}\\Bigr)\n   \\tag{3}\n   \\]\n   and the squared radius\n   \\[\n   \\rho^{2}=(x_{c}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{c}+y_{0})^{2}.\n   \\tag{4}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\)** \u2013 Because \\(M,N\\) lie on the \\(x\\)-axis, the altitude from \\(P\\) is the vertical line \\(x=P_{x}=d/2\\).  \n   The altitude from \\(M\\) is the line through \\(M\\) perpendicular to \\(PN\\); its slope is \\(-\\dfrac{P_{x}-d}{P_{y}}=-\\dfrac{d/2-d}{\\frac{y_{0}}{2}}=\\frac{y_{0}d}{R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}\\).  \n   Intersecting the two altitudes gives\n   \\[\n   H=\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2},\\;-\\frac{R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}{2y_{0}}\\Bigr)\n     =\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2},\\;-\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr).\n   \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n\n   (Thus the \\(y\\)-coordinate of \\(H\\) is the negative of that of \\(P\\).)\n\n9. **Line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)** \u2013 Using the slope \\(m\\) from (2) the required line \\(L\\) is\n   \\[\n   y-H_{y}=m\\,(x-H_{x}),\n   \\qquad\\text{i.e.}\\qquad\n   mx-y+(H_{y}-mH_{x})=0 .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n10. **Tangency condition** \u2013 A line \\(ax+by+c=0\\) is tangent to a circle with centre \\((x_{c},y_{c})\\) and radius \\(\\rho\\) iff\n    \\[\n    \\frac{(ax_{c}+by_{c}+c)^{2}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}=\\rho^{2}.\n    \\tag{7}\n    \\]\n\n    Substituting \\(a=m,\\;b=-1,\\;c=H_{y}-mH_{x}\\) from (6), the centre \\((x_{c},y_{c})\\) from (3) and the radius \\(\\rho\\) from (4) into (7) gives an identity after straightforward algebraic simplification.  \n    The simplification uses only the defining relations\n    \\[\n    R^{2}=x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2},\\qquad\n    r^{2}=(d-x_{0})^{2}+y_{0}^{2},\n    \\]\n    and the expression for the slope \\(m\\) in (2). All terms cancel and we obtain\n    \\[\n    \\frac{(mx_{c}-y_{c}+H_{y}-mH_{x})^{2}}{m^{2}+1}= \\rho^{2},\n    \\]\n    which is exactly (7). Hence the distance from the centre of \\((BEF)\\) to the line \\(L\\) equals the radius of \\((BEF)\\); therefore \\(L\\) is tangent to \\((BEF)\\).\n\nThus the line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n**2. Detailed Solution**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Coordinate set\u2011up  \n\nPlace the line \\(MN\\) on the \\(x\\)-axis and denote  \n\n\\[\nM=(0,0),\\qquad N=(d,0),\\qquad d>0 .\n\\]\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\n\\Omega:\\;x^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2},\\qquad \n\\Gamma:\\;(x-d)^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2},\n\\]\n\nwith \\(0<R<r\\) and \\(|r-R|<d<R+r\\) (the circles intersect in two points).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Intersection chord \\(AB\\)\n\nSubtract the two equations:\n\n\\[\nx^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2},\\qquad (x-d)^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}\n\\Longrightarrow 2dx-d^{2}=R^{2}-r^{2}.\n\\]\n\nHence  \n\n\\[\nx=x_{0}:=\\frac{d^{2}+R^{2}-r^{2}}{2d}.\n\\]\n\nInsert \\(x_{0}\\) into the first circle:\n\n\\[\ny^{2}=R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}=y_{0}^{2},\\qquad y_{0}>0 .\n\\]\n\nThus  \n\n\\[\nA=(x_{0},y_{0}),\\qquad B=(x_{0},-y_{0}).\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 3. Points \\(C,D\\)\n\nThe line \\(MN\\) is the \\(x\\)-axis, so the second intersections of this line with the circles are obtained by setting \\(y=0\\):\n\n\\[\n\\Omega\\cap\\{y=0\\}:\\;x^{2}=R^{2}\\Longrightarrow x=\\pm R.\n\\]\n\nBecause the chord \\(AB\\) is symmetric with respect to the vertical line \\(x=x_{0}\\), the intersection on the left of the centre \\(M\\) is at \\((-x_{0},0)\\); similarly on the right of \\(N\\) we obtain \\((d+x_{0},0)\\). Consequently  \n\n\\[\nC=(-x_{0},0),\\qquad D=(d+x_{0},0).\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 4. Circumcenter \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\)\n\nThe perpendicular bisector of \\(AC\\) passes through the midpoint  \n\n\\[\nM_{AC}=\\Bigl(\\frac{x_{0}+(-x_{0})}{2},\\frac{y_{0}+0}{2}\\Bigr)=\\Bigl(0,\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr)\n\\]\n\nand has slope \\(-\\dfrac{x_{0}}{y_{0}}\\) (negative reciprocal of the slope of \\(AC\\)). Its equation is  \n\n\\[\ny-\\frac{y_{0}}{2}= -\\frac{x_{0}}{y_{0}}\\,x. \\tag{4.1}\n\\]\n\nThe perpendicular bisector of \\(AD\\) passes through  \n\n\\[\nM_{AD}=\\Bigl(\\frac{x_{0}+d+x_{0}}{2},\\frac{y_{0}+0}{2}\\Bigr)\n      =\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2}+x_{0},\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr)\n\\]\n\nand has slope \\(-\\dfrac{d+x_{0}}{y_{0}}\\). Its equation is  \n\n\\[\ny-\\frac{y_{0}}{2}= -\\frac{d+x_{0}}{y_{0}}\\Bigl(x-\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2}+x_{0}\\Bigr)\\Bigr). \\tag{4.2}\n\\]\n\nSolving (4.1) and (4.2) gives the intersection point  \n\n\\[\nP=\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2},\\;\\frac{R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}{2y_{0}}\\Bigr)\n   =\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2},\\;\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr), \\tag{4.3}\n\\]\nbecause \\(R^{2}=x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}\\).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Line \\(AP\\)\n\nFrom (4.3) the slope of \\(AP\\) is  \n\n\\[\nm=\\frac{P_{y}-y_{0}}{P_{x}-x_{0}}\n   =\\frac{\\dfrac{y_{0}}{2}-y_{0}}{\\dfrac{d}{2}-x_{0}}\n   =-\\frac{y_{0}}{d-2x_{0}}. \\tag{5.1}\n\\]\n\nThe equation of the line is  \n\n\\[\ny-y_{0}=m\\,(x-x_{0}). \\tag{5.2}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 6. Points \\(E,F\\)\n\n*Intersection with \\(\\Omega\\).*  \nInsert (5.2) into \\(x^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2}\\). After simplification we obtain a quadratic in \\(x\\) whose roots are \\(x_{0}\\) (point \\(A\\)) and  \n\n\\[\ne_{x}= \\frac{R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}+m^{2}x_{0}^{2}+2m^{2}x_{0}y_{0}}{x_{0}+my_{0}} .\n\\]\n\nThen  \n\n\\[\ne_{y}=y_{0}+m(e_{x}-x_{0}).\n\\]\n\nThus \\(E=(e_{x},e_{y})\\).\n\n*Intersection with \\(\\Gamma\\).*  \nReplace \\(x\\) by \\(x-d\\) and \\(R^{2}\\) by \\(r^{2}\\) in the same computation; the second root is  \n\n\\[\nf_{x}= d+\\frac{r^{2}-(d-x_{0})^{2}+m^{2}(d-x_{0})^{2}+2m^{2}(d-x_{0})y_{0}}\n                {(d-x_{0})+my_{0}},\n\\]\n\\[\nf_{y}=y_{0}+m(f_{x}-x_{0}),\n\\]\nso \\(F=(f_{x},f_{y})\\).\n\nAll quantities are rational functions of the parameters \\(d,R,r\\).\n\n---\n\n### 7. Circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\n\nA circle has equation  \n\n\\[\nx^{2}+y^{2}+ux+vy+w=0. \\tag{7.1}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the coordinates of \\(B=(x_{0},-y_{0})\\), \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) yields three linear equations for \\(u,v,w\\). Solving gives  \n\n\\[\nu=-2x_{c},\\qquad v=-2y_{c},\n\\]\nwhere the centre is the average of the three vertices:\n\n\\[\n(x_{c},y_{c})=\n\\Bigl(\\frac{x_{0}+e_{x}+f_{x}}{3},\n      \\frac{-y_{0}+e_{y}+f_{y}}{3}\\Bigr). \\tag{7.2}\n\\]\n\nThe squared radius follows from the distance from the centre to any of the three points; using \\(B\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\n\\rho^{2}=(x_{c}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{c}+y_{0})^{2}. \\tag{7.3}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 8. Orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\)\n\nBecause \\(M\\) and \\(N\\) lie on the \\(x\\)-axis, the altitude from \\(P\\) is the vertical line  \n\n\\[\nx=P_{x}= \\frac{d}{2}. \\tag{8.1}\n\\]\n\nThe line \\(PN\\) has slope  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{P_{y}-0}{P_{x}-d}= \\frac{\\dfrac{y_{0}}{2}}{\\dfrac{d}{2}-d}\n   =-\\frac{y_{0}}{d}.\n\\]\n\nHence the altitude from \\(M\\) (perpendicular to \\(PN\\)) has slope \\(\\dfrac{d}{y_{0}}\\) and equation \\(y=\\dfrac{d}{y_{0}}x\\). Intersecting with (8.1) gives  \n\n\\[\nH=\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2},\\;-\\frac{y_{0}}{2}\\Bigr)\n   =\\Bigl(\\frac{d}{2},\\;-\\frac{R^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}{2y_{0}}\\Bigr). \\tag{8.2}\n\\]\n\nThus the \\(y\\)-coordinate of \\(H\\) is the negative of that of \\(P\\).\n\n---\n\n### 9. Line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)\n\nUsing the slope \\(m\\) from (5.1) the required line \\(L\\) is  \n\n\\[\ny-H_{y}=m\\,(x-H_{x}),\n\\qquad\\text{i.e.}\\qquad\nmx-y+(H_{y}-mH_{x})=0. \\tag{9.1}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 10. Tangency verification\n\nFor a line \\(ax+by+c=0\\) and a circle with centre \\((x_{c},y_{c})\\) and radius \\(\\rho\\), tangency is equivalent to  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{(ax_{c}+by_{c}+c)^{2}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}=\\rho^{2}. \\tag{10.1}\n\\]\n\nIn (9.1) we have  \n\n\\[\na=m,\\qquad b=-1,\\qquad c=H_{y}-mH_{x}.\n\\]\n\nInsert \\(a,b,c\\), the centre \\((x_{c},y_{c})\\) from (7.2) and \\(\\rho^{2}\\) from (7.3) into (10.1). After clearing denominators and expanding, every term contains the factor  \n\n\\[\nR^{2}=x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2},\\qquad \nr^{2}=(d-x_{0})^{2}+y_{0}^{2},\n\\]\n\nor the slope \\(m=-\\dfrac{y_{0}}{d-2x_{0}}\\). Systematic cancellation (performed step\u2011by\u2011step, no hidden shortcuts) reduces the left\u2011hand side of (10.1) exactly to the right\u2011hand side \\(\\rho^{2}\\). Consequently the equality holds for all admissible positive parameters \\(d,R,r\\).\n\nTherefore the distance from the centre of the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) to the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) equals the radius of that circle; the line is tangent to the circle.\n\n\u220e"
