nd a **Critical Error** (second part).\n\n### Lemma\u202f5 (Perpendicularity to \\(BF\\))\n\n> \u201cFrom (2) we have \\(AP\\parallel AF\\). Together with (3) this yields \\(AP\\perp BF\\)\u2026 Reflection across the midpoint \\(M_{0}\\) preserves angles, so the reflected line \\(\\ell_{H}\\) through\u202fH \u2026 also satisfies \\(\\ell_{H}\\perp BF\\).\u201d\n\n- **Analysis:** This lemma rests on the false statements (2) and (3) from Lemma\u202f2, so the derived perpendicularity is baseless \u2013 a **critical error**. Moreover, the claim that reflection across \\(M_{0}\\) preserves angles is true, but the step that the reflected line remains parallel to \\(AP\\) is not justified because the earlier identification of the reflected line itself is built on the erroneous reflection property from Lemma\u202f4. Hence the whole lemma is invalid.  \n\n- **Classification:** **Critical Error** (propagation of earlier errors) and **Justification Gap** (unproved preservation of parallelism).\n\n### Lemma\u202f6 (Remaining step \u2013 tangency)\n\n> \u201cWe have shown that \\(\\ell\\perp BF\\)\u2026 the fact that \\(\\ell\\) is perpendicular to \\(BF\\) does **not** by itself guarantee that \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to \\((BEF)\\)\u2026 an additional argument is required.\u201d\n\n- **Analysis:** The author correctly acknowledges that the proof is incomplete. However, because all preceding lemmas are flawed, the statement \u201cwe have shown that \\(\\ell\\perp BF\\)\u201d is false. The lemma therefore does not provide any valid information toward the final claim.  \n\n- **Classification:** **Justification Gap** (the step is admitted incomplete) and **Critical Error** (the premise is false).\n\n### Overall Assessment\n\nThe solution fails at the very first step by misidentifying the radical axis, which invalidates Lemma\u202f1. Subsequent lemmas rely on this and on other incorrect geometric assertions (homothety mapping, orthocenter reflection). Consequently the core claim\u201