een $MN$ and the angles at $B$ of triangle $BEF$. This statement is false.\n\n3. **Conclusion:** \u201cSince $H'$ lies on the external symmedian \u2026 the line through $H'$ perpendicular to $MN$ coincides with the tangent at $B$ to $\\omega_{BEF}$.\u201d  \n   *Critical Error:* Because the previous two claims are false, the conclusion that $H'$ lies on the external symmedian is baseless. Hence the final tangency claim is unsupported.\n\n---\n\n#### Final step (undoing the inversion)\n\nThe solution claims that undoing the inversion maps the tangent line back to the required parallel line.  \n*Critical Error:* Since the inversion mapping was incorrectly described, this reversal is invalid.\n\n---\n\n### Overall Assessment\nThe solution hinges on an incorrect Lemma\u202f1, misuses inversion (incorrect images of circles, false preservation of parallelism, and false invariance of $B$ and $\\omega_{BEF}$), and contains several unfounded geometric claims (e.g., $APMN$ being a rectangle, $MN$ as an external angle bisector). These constitute **Critical Errors** that break the logical chain of the proof. Consequently the argument does not constitute a valid solution to the problem."
