use \\(A,P,O\\) are collinear (proved in step\u202f4).  \n   * (ii) **Collinearity \\(A,P,O\\).** Since \\(O\\) lies on the line \\(\\ell\\) (the centre line of the coaxial pencil) and \\(AB\\perp\\ell\\), the radius \\(OB\\) is perpendicular to \\(AB\\). The line \\(AP\\) passes through the midpoint \\(K\\) of \\(CD\\) and is perpendicular to \\(CD\\subset MN\\); because \\(MN\\) is also perpendicular to \\(\\ell\\), we obtain \\(AP\\parallel\\ell\\). Consequently \\(A,P,O\\) are collinear.\n\n   With (i) and (ii) we have that the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is parallel to \\(AO\\).\n\n4. **Tangency condition.**  \n   For a circle, a line is tangent at a point \\(X\\) iff it is perpendicular to the radius drawn to \\(X\\). By (ii) the line \\(AO\\) is perpendicular to the radius \\(OB\\) of the circum\u2011circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). Therefore the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) (which is parallel to \\(AO\\)) is perpendicular to \\(OB\\) and hence tangent to the circum\u2011circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) at the point \\(B\\).\n\nAll steps are proved rigorously below.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**2. Detailed Solution**\n\nLet  \n\n* \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\) be the given circles with centres \\(M\\) and \\(N\\) (\\(r_{\\Omega}<r_{\\Gamma}\\));\n* \\(A,B\\) their two intersection points;\n* \\(C\\in\\Omega\\) and \\(D\\in\\Gamma\\) the points on the line \\(MN\\) with order \\(C-M-N-D\\);\n* \\(P\\) the circum\u2011centre of \\(\\triangle ACD\\);\n* \\(E\\neq A\\) the second intersection of line \\(AP\\) with \\(\\Omega\\);\n* \\(F\\neq A\\) the second intersection of line \\(AP\\) with \\(\\Gamma\\);\n* \\(H\\) the orthocentre of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).\n\nWe must show that the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circum\u2011circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma 1 (Coaxial pencil)\n\nAll