f \\(\\triangle PMN\\))\n\nLet \\(K\\) be the midpoint of \\(MN\\). Then \\(K\\) is the circum\u2011centre of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) and  \n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{PH}\\parallel\\overrightarrow{PA}.\n\\]\n\n*Proof.*  \nBecause \\(K\\) is the midpoint of \\(MN\\), it lies on the perpendicular bisector of \\(MN\\). The line \\(AP\\) is the perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) (Lemma\u202f2, part\u202f2) and \\(CD\\subset MN\\); consequently \\(AP\\) is also the perpendicular bisector of \\(MN\\). Hence \\(K\\) lies on \\(AP\\) and is equidistant from \\(M\\) and \\(N\\). Moreover \\(KP=KA\\) (as \\(K\\) is on the perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) and \\(P\\) is the centre of the circle through \\(A,C,D\\)). Thus \\(K\\) is equidistant from the three vertices \\(P,M,N\\); therefore \\(K\\) is the circum\u2011centre of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).\n\nIn any triangle, the vector from a vertex to the orthocentre is parallel to the vector from the opposite vertex to the circum\u2011centre. Applying this to \\(\\triangle PMN\\) with circum\u2011centre \\(K\\) gives \\(\\overrightarrow{PH}\\parallel\\overrightarrow{PK}\\). Since \\(K\\) lies on \\(AP\\) (as shown above), \\(\\overrightarrow{PK}\\) is collinear with \\(\\overrightarrow{PA}\\). Hence \\(\\overrightarrow{PH}\\parallel\\overrightarrow{PA}\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n### Lemma 4 (The required tangency)\n\nThe line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circum\u2011circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) at \\(B\\).\n\n*Proof.*  \nBy Lemma\u202f3 the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is also parallel to \\(PA\\). Lemma\u202f2 (part\u202f2) tells us that \\(A,P,O\\) are collinear, so this line is parallel to \\(AO\\). Lemma\u202f2 (part\u202f3) gives \\(AO\\perp OB\\).  \n\nFor a circle, a line is tangent at a point precisely when it is perpendicular to the radius drawn to that point. The radius of the circum\u2011circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) drawn to \\(B\\) is \\(OB\\). Hence any line perpendicular to \\(OB\\) is tangent to that circle at \\(B\\). Since the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is parallel to \\(AO\\) and \\(AO\\perp OB\\), the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is perpendicular to \\(OB\\) and therefore tangent to the circum\u2011circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) at \\(B\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n### Conclusion\n\nAll lemmas have been proved rigorously and together they establish that the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). \u220e"
