llel to \\(AP\\) touches the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) at \\(B\\)\u201d follows from Lemma\u202f5, which itself is invalid. Hence the overall solution fails to prove the required result.\n\n**Overall Assessment:** The solution contains multiple critical errors (most notably the false claim that \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) lie on the common chord \\(AB\\)) and several unjustified steps. Consequently, the proof is not rigorous and does not establish the theorem."
