rallel to \\(AP\\) is not proved; multiple lines can have the same distance from a point to a circle (the two tangents). Hence the argument is incomplete.\n\n7. **Conclusion**  \n   The solution\u2019s final statement \u201cSince all steps are justified, the statement is proved\u201d is false because several critical errors and numerous justification gaps have been identified. The proof does not establish the required tangency.\n\n**Overall Assessment:** The solution fails to provide a correct and rigorous proof. The initial misidentification of geometric relations (particularly the claim \\(AP\\perp CD\\)) propagates through the argument, and many later steps are either unjustified or outright incorrect. Consequently, the solution is invalid."
