n Gap)\n\n---\n\n#### Lemma\u202f7 (Simson line tangency theorem)\n\n> \u201cThe Simson line of a point on the circumcircle is tangent to the circumcircle of its pedal triangle.\u201d\n\n**Issue Identified \u2013 Justification Gap**\n\n* The lemma is quoted as a known theorem without proof. In a grading context, citing a theorem is acceptable **provided** the theorem\u2019s hypotheses are verified for the current configuration. The solution does not verify that point \\(A\\) indeed lies on the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) (this was the content of Lemma\u202f4, which is false). Hence the applicability of the theorem is not established. \u2705 (Justification Gap)\n\n---\n\n#### Completion of the proof\n\nThe final step combines Lemmas\u202f5,\u202f6,\u202f7. Since Lemmas\u202f5 and\u202f4 are false and Lemma\u202f6 is insufficiently justified, the conclusion does not follow from the presented arguments.\n\n---\n\n### Overall Assessment\nThe solution collapses at **Lemma\u202f2**, where an incorrect claim about the location of the circumcenter \\(P\\) is made. This error propagates to Lemmas\u202f4,\u202f5,\u202f6 and invalidates the entire argument. Additional gaps in justification (Lemmas\u202f6 and\u202f7) further weaken the proof. Consequently, the solution is **invalid** due to critical errors."
